#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Nanopore full-length 16S microbiome pipeline (abundance + diversity)

Inputs
------
1) Per-sample taxa tables:
   *_subsampled_taxa.txt files inside treatment folders (e.g., adult_control/)

   Expected tab-separated columns (no header):
   taxonomy <tab> count <tab> read_ids

2) Rarefied/subsampled count table for diversity (CSV):
   rows = samples, columns = taxa/ASVs/OTUs (counts), index_col=0

Outputs
-------
- Stacked barplots (individual samples + mean per treatment) at genus/species
- Alpha diversity boxplots (Shannon, Simpson) per metric (one plot each)
- Beta diversity PCoA plots (Bray-Curtis, Jaccard) per metric (one plot each)
- Global + pairwise statistics tables + significant summary report (FDR on all post-hoc p-values)

Note: This script assumes sample names contain treatment keywords (see extract_treatment()).
"""

